{
  "about": "The features the design requires, each tied to rule IDs in docs/design/rules.md and to the evidence the scan looks for. Priority is not stored here: it is computed from G1, G2, G3 and G5 through each feature's `terms` and `milestone`, which must name words those rules use. `build` marks a feature the goal agent may write itself; without it the gap goes to its owner through the producer.",
  "not_tracked": {
    "P1": "pillar: a tie-breaker for judgment calls, not a system",
    "P2": "pillar", "P3": "pillar", "P4": "pillar", "P5": "pillar",
    "F2": "process: clip first, then frame data (Clip Matcher, Movesmith)",
    "F5": "process: no hand-keyed animation",
    "F6": "process: how assets are generated and sourced",
    "M2": "pacing target, read from harness results by Sparring Partner",
    "S1": "tone, judged by the Rules Lawyer on story text",
    "V1": "art direction, checked by Asset Smith's acceptance",
    "V9": "stages and music: generated and sourced assets",
    "G1": "scope: read by the agent to rank work, not a feature",
    "G2": "scope", "G3": "scope", "G4": "scope: week-1 retarget gate", "G5": "scope: schedule"
  },
